{
  "assembly_notes": "Mobile industrial work table. The grounded `frame` part is the welded post-and-rail structure: four posts, perimeter rails and the storage bay's own rails. Four braked swivel casters hang from the post feet and are identity-fixed: a `caster_swivel` turns CONTINUOUS about +z in a bored king-pin boss, a `caster_wheel` spins CONTINUOUS about the yoke's local +y between two yoke cheeks, and a `caster_brake` pedal swings REVOLUTE about the same local axis onto the tread. All four share one motion_qc_repeat_group. The `worktop` is a separate part so the leg_form slot can make it either FIXED at the working height or PRISMATIC over the telescopic posts' travel; top_surface only changes what that part is made of and how its edge is formed. storage_module fills the bay with storage_level_count items - fixed shelf panels, sliding drawer trays with real bilateral runners, or sliding pegboard trays under a perforated back panel - and every candidate derives its level pitch from the same bay height. table_length_m, table_depth_m and table_height_m are honest continuous parameters that derive rail spans, caster track, bay height, level pitch, drawer travel and post travel; palette, perforations and glue lines are non-core. bench_accessory adds one source-backed bench fitting on the frame's rear brackets or front rail - a display arm with its own REVOLUTE tilt, a keyboard tray on PRISMATIC side runners, or a fixed equipment box - none of which touch the caster or storage chains. side_bracing leaves the side bays open on their rails or fills each one with two crossed flat bars on the bay's own diagonal.",
